openharmony-sig/deveco-cli
--------------------------
https://gitcode.com/openharmony-sig/deveco-cli
Copyright (c) 2026 Huawei Device Co., Ltd.
Licensed under the MIT License.

Portions of packages/core/src/harmonyos/ are adapted from this project — the
Huawei developer account sign-in flow and the AppGallery Connect certificate and
provisioning-profile client used by `oniro-app sign --harmonyos`. Each adapted
file carries a header naming its upstream origin; a file-by-file map, the list
of deviations, and the full MIT license text are in
packages/core/src/harmonyos/NOTICE.md.

packages/core/vendor/deveco-cli/arkts-check.cjs, which `oniro-app check arkts`
runs, is deveco-cli 1.3.10's packages/cli/src/resources/arkts-check.cjs (commit
99e3725fc2c5), changed to take the SDK directory with `--sdk` and the
HarmonyOS API directory with `--hms` instead of locating DevEco Studio, and to
let `--fix` export a declaration from a file that exports nothing yet. Its
header lists the changes, and the MIT license text sits beside it in LICENSE.

The launch smoke check (packages/core/src/hdc/smoke.ts) and its blank-screen
test (packages/core/src/image/hash.ts) follow deveco-cli's smoke inspector
(packages/cli/src/smoke/, notably screen-phash.ts): wait for the process,
capture the screen, crop the status and navigation bars, and compare a DCT
perceptual hash with a flat frame's, a distance of 10 bits or less meaning
blank. Both files are reimplementations that carry a header naming the origin;
they work on greyscale decoded by the caller, and add a variance condition and
a background-share measure to the hash test.

